      "observed": "R6 is listed with value \"10M\" in the netlist and 10Meg in the SPICE deck, while it is used as the I2C pull-up from DISP_SCL to VCC.",
      "expected": "R6 should be 10 kΩ, as specified for the DISP_SCL pull-up to VCC.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`DISP_SCL`: U2 pin 34 (`PB13`) — R6 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pin 18 (`D0`)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R6\")\n      (value \"10M\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R6 DISP_SCL VCC 10Meg"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The display I2C SCL line would have an extremely weak pull-up, causing slow or failed rise times and likely preventing reliable SSD1306 communication.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "One clear anomaly was found: R6, the DISP_SCL I2C pull-up, is 10 MΩ / 10Meg instead of the specified 10 kΩ, which would severely compromise or break the display bus."
}

